{"id":156183,"accession_number":"1992.1","share_license_status":"CC0","tombstone":"Summer Mountains (after Dong Yuan [active c. 937–75]), 1290–1354. Attributed to Huang Gongwang (Chinese, 1269–1354). Hanging scroll; ink and slight color on silk; image: 131.7 x 55.6 cm (51 7/8 x 21 7/8 in.); overall: 257.4 x 71.2 cm (101 5/16 x 28 1/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cornelia Blakemore Warner Bequest, by exchange, and Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1992.1","current_location":null,"title":"Summer Mountains (after Dong Yuan [active c. 937–75])","creation_date":"1290–1354","creation_date_earliest":1290,"creation_date_latest":1354,"artists_tags":["male"],"culture":["China, Yuan dynasty (1271-1368)"],"technique":"hanging scroll; ink and slight color on silk","support_materials":[],"department":"Chinese Art","collection":"ASIAN - Hanging scroll","type":"Painting","measurements":"Image: 131.7 x 55.6 cm (51 7/8 x 21 7/8 in.); Overall: 257.4 x 71.2 cm (101 5/16 x 28 1/16 in.)","dimensions":{"image":{"height":1.317,"height_inch":51,"height_inch_fraction":0.875,"width":0.556,"width_inch":21,"width_inch_fraction":0.875},"overall":{"height":2.574,"height_inch":101,"height_inch_fraction":0.3125,"width":0.712,"width_inch":28,"width_inch_fraction":0.0625}},"state_of_the_work":null,"edition_of_the_work":null,"copyright":null,"inscriptions":[{"inscription":"","inscription_translation":"Yifeng dao ren [Huang Gongwang] [painted this] in imitation of Beiyuan's [Dong Yuan's] \"[missing character] Mountains\"","inscription_remark":null,"sortorder":1},{"inscription":null,"inscription_translation":"On the 16th, in 1599, I traded Cao Fenzhi for this. Now, in 1600, also on the 16th, I have rehung the scroll to study it. Qichang.","inscription_remark":"Inscription formerly on the paintings' mounting by Dong Qichang 董其昌 (1555–1636)","sortorder":2},{"inscription":"【印】一峰道人","inscription_translation":"Seal of the artist: \"Yifeng dao ren\"","inscription_remark":null,"sortorder":3}],"exhib